  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}$, and $\\vec{c}$ be three non-zero, non-coplanar vectors such that $\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} + \\vec{c} = 0$. The value of $\\vec{a}^2 + \\vec{b}^2 + \\vec{c}^2$ equals:",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "$\\vec{a} + \\vec{b} + \\vec{c} = 0$.<br /><br />Squaring both sides gives $(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c})^2=0$.<br /><br />$\\vec{a}^2 + \\vec{b}^2 + \\vec{c}^2 + 2(\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} + \\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{c} + \\vec{c}\\cdot\\vec{a}) = 0$.<br /><br />Hence $\\vec{a}^2 + \\vec{b}^2 + \\vec{c}^2 = -2(\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} + \\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{c} + \\vec{c}\\cdot\\vec{a})$.",
